# Personalizing Psychotherapy for Suicide Risk Reduction

Machine learning analysis of electronic health record data to optimize psychotherapy selection for patients at suicide risk.

## Overview

This repository contains code for developing and validating machine learning models that predict suicide risk improvement across different psychotherapy modalities. Using data from a large national behavioral health system (n=5,986 treatment episodes), we train XGBoost models to match individual patient characteristics to optimal evidence-based psychotherapies.

**Key findings:** Models suggest potential risk reduction in 26.9% of patients through optimized therapy selection, with a number needed to treat of 156.

